          'Alternative – only one of the two: entweder A oder B (either A or B). Double negation – neither of the two: weder A noch B (neither A nor B = not A and not B either). Careful: weder … noch already negates by itself; an additional nicht or kein is wrong. When only parts of a sentence are linked, there is no comma before oder and noch.',
